  <running_head>P. Rami</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Cap.</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">portet. Comp. ἀπήχεη sufficit: ἀπέχεη</l>
    <l n="2">sufficiebat: ἀπεχέησθ sufficiet:</l>
    <l n="3">ἀπέχεησε suffecit.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">πρέπει decet, ἔπρεπε, πρέπειν.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">συμφώνει convenit, συμφώνε, συμφώνειν.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">φιλεῖ solet, ἀ φιλέω.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Aliquando etiam infectum est pro</l>
    <l n="8">præsenti, ut ἔδει, ἔπρεπε, pro δεῖ, πρέπει.</l>
    <l n="9">Sic horist. εἴωθε confuevit, solet: πέφυκε</l>
    <l n="10">natura fit.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Formæ secundæ sunt: συνδέχεται acci-</l>
    <l n="12">dit: ἐπιρχεται succurrit: unde ἐπῆλθε, in</l>
    <l n="13">mentem venit, lubitum est. Sic</l>
    <l n="14">λέγεται dicitur, fertur: λείπεται relinquitur,</l>
    <l n="15">superest.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">εἰμάρται &amp; πέπρωται, in fatis est.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">ἠκούσται auditum est.</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">ἐγνώσται decretum est.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">εἴρηται dictum est.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">εἰρήσθω dictum fit: εἰρήσεται, dicetur.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Greek polytonic forms are approximate; several accents and breathings are uncertain and may differ from the print. Words with [?] were not clearly legible.</notes>
